# The LightGBM booster is a TEXT file that must keep LF endings. With
# core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) git rewrites it to CRLF on checkout
# and LightGBM's parser then fails with
#
#   [LightGBM] [Fatal] Model format error, expect a tree here. met ...
#
# which adapter/ml_source.py catches: every tower silently falls back to the
# physical noisy-OR index, `condition` reads null, and nothing at startup says
# the served model is missing. The failure is invisible unless you read the
# booster's own stderr.
#
# Checked out on Linux the file was always fine, so this only ever bit Windows
# checkouts — which is exactly the sort of difference that makes a local
# result and a deployed result disagree for no visible reason.
data/malaysia/maintenance_model.txt -text

# Same reason, pre-emptively: any future booster or model export.
*.lgb -text
